  "body": "Companion PR to [whatwg/html PR](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/13326) (integrating `Document-Isolation-Policy` from\nhttps://wicg.github.io/document-isolation-policy/).\n### Summary of changes\n- Replicates the effect of on subresource fetches of COEP (credentialless, require-corp) for Document Isolation Polciy.\n- Adds reporting when Document Isolation Policy blocks subresource loads.\n\n*(Note: `TEMP` commit adds temporary HTML anchors to `fetch.bs` so Bikeshed previews stay green; drop\nthat commit after the companion `whatwg/html` PR merges and spec-data updates.)*\n\n### Known pre-existing caveat\nAs with `Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: credentialless`, `HTTP-network-or-cache fetch` does not yet\nexplicitly separate HTTP cache entries stored from credentialed vs. uncredentialed fetches\n(see `html/document-isolation-policy/credentialless-cache.tentative.window.js`).\n### Merge order\n1. Merge the companion `whatwg/html` PR first so its exported definitions land in HTML/Shepherd.\n2. Wait for Bikeshed spec-data rebuild, drop the temporary `<pre class=anchors>` commit, and merge this PR.\n### Checklist\n- [ ] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * Chromium (implemented)\n   * WebKit / Gecko: …\n- [ ] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/tree/master/html/document-isolation-policy (currently `.tentative`; follow-up WPT PR will remove `.tentative`)\n- [ ] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: …\n   * Gecko: …\n   * WebKit: …\n   * Deno: N/A\n- [ ] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: …\n- [x] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/fetch/1981.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 25, 2026, 5:27 PM UTC (ca41826)\">Preview</a> | <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/fetch/1981/d7fc0fd...ca41826.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 25, 2026, 5:27 PM UTC (ca41826)\">Diff</a>",
